# VoiceVision Core Pipeline - VoicePipeline.process()
# Source: src/voicevision/pipeline.py

The VoicePipeline class wires the complete voice loop:
1. VAD: WebrtcVadBackend segments 16kHz mono PCM16 audio
2. STT: WhisperCppBackend transcribes via whisper.cpp CLI
3. LLM: LlamaCppBackend uses supervised llama-server daemon
4. Filter: Strips qwen3 reasoning traces (<think>...</think>)
5. TTS: PiperBackend synthesizes speech (currently broken)

Listen mode (src/voicevision/listen.py):
- Single-shot: captures one utterance, transcribes, prints to stdout
- Wake word: "Olá Ambrósio" default, configurable via VOICEVISION_HOTWORDS
- Continuous: --continuous flag loops until Ctrl+C
- Pre-roll buffer: circular buffer captures audio before wake word
- History: optional transcript logging to ~/.voicevision/history.jsonl

The pipeline is the single integration point - VAD→STT→LLM→filter→TTS